# hornero-nest: original HorneroOS artwork (MIT, like this repository): a rufous hornero
# perched on its clay-oven nest, with a lit doorway and a little aerial.
# full 34x40 px (20 terminal rows). One character = one pixel; two pixel rows = one terminal row
# (half blocks). Legend lines start with "@ <char> <ANSI SGR foreground>".
# Colours are terminal palette ROLES, never RGB, so every Signal theme and
# every Hornero Chromatic palette repaints the bird: 33 amber (plumage),
# 93 bright amber (belly, wing edge, lamp), 37 pale (throat), 90 slate (nest
# stone, beak), 36 cyan (cue), 32 green (LED), 35 rose (blush).
# "none" = a hole that shows the terminal background (the eye).
# Regenerate the outputs with scripts/gen-fastfetch-logo.py.
@ a 33
@ b 93
@ c 37
@ s 90
@ k 36
@ l 32
@ r 35
@ e none
